Turn asio's threads on for MinGW consumers

asio enables threads only when it sees _REENTRANT, _MT or a similar macro.
MinGW GCC predefines _REENTRANT. Clang predefines none of them, and _MT
only appears once a CRT header has been included, so on CLANG64 a unit
whose first include is Link gets asio's null_thread, and the first timer
aborts with "thread: The attempted operation is not supported". Define
ASIO_HAS_THREADS for every user of Ableton::Link on MinGW. The MinGW-w64
CRT is always multithreaded, so this is what asio should detect anyway.

Upstream: not submitted (MSYS2's asio has the same fix pending)
Applies-to: all environments

--- a/cmake_include/ConfigureAbletonLink.cmake
+++ b/cmake_include/ConfigureAbletonLink.cmake
@@ -44,6 +44,13 @@
         iphlpapi
         ws2_32
       )
+      # asio turns threads on from _REENTRANT or _MT. Clang predefines
+      # neither, and _MT only comes with the first CRT header, so a unit
+      # that includes Link first would get asio without threads.
+      set_property(TARGET Ableton::Link APPEND PROPERTY
+        INTERFACE_COMPILE_DEFINITIONS
+        ASIO_HAS_THREADS=1
+      )
     endif()
     elseif(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES "Linux|kFreeBSD|GNU|Android")
       set_property(TARGET Ableton::Link APPEND PROPERTY
